-- UK: The Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018 (S.I. 2018/506) -- INDEPENDENT TESTS.
-- A DRAFT. Not for use as advice.
--
-- Written by a session that did not see the encoding being built. Every expected
-- value was decided from the deposited sources (uksi-2018-506.txt and eur-2018-151.txt,
-- both role `aid`: Lex re-serves of legislation.gov.uk text, NOT the official register)
-- and written down in tests-independent-answers-first.md BEFORE the encoding was opened;
-- the baseline (nis-seat.l4) and the type declarations were then read only to learn
-- names. No expectation was adjusted to match the code. A failing assertion here is a
-- finding, left failing on purpose; each one carries a comment naming the provision.
-- Line pins "txt:N" are lines of registers/source-bundle/uksi-2018-506.txt.

§ `Independent fixtures`

`indep: yes` MEANS `yes, it is`
`indep: no` MEANS `no, it is not`
`indep: cannot say` MEANS `I cannot say`

`indep: RDSP duty` MEANS `regulation 12(3): an RDSP's incident`
`indep: OES duty` MEANS `regulation 11(1): an OES's NIS incident`
`indep: 12(9) duty` MEANS `regulation 12(9): an OES's notice of an incident affecting an RDSP it relies on`

`indep: reading late is a 12(3) failure` MEANS `reading A: a late notice is a failure to notify under regulation 12(3)`
`indep: reading 12(6) not listed` MEANS `reading B: lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`

`indep: no EN` MEANS `no enforcement notice was served on me`
`indep: EN no steps` MEANS `an enforcement notice was served on me but required no steps`
`indep: EN steps taken` MEANS `an enforcement notice required steps and I took them within its period`
`indep: EN steps not taken` MEANS `an enforcement notice required steps and I did not take them within its period`

`indep: significant` MEANS `the authority determines it has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
`indep: not significant` MEANS `the authority determines it does not meet that test`
`indep: undetermined` MEANS `the authority has not yet determined this`

GIVETH A DATE
`indep: 2026-03-02` MEANS Date 2 3 2026
GIVETH A DATE
`indep: 2026-03-05` MEANS Date 5 3 2026
GIVETH A DATE
`indep: 2026-03-06` MEANS Date 6 3 2026
GIVETH A DATE
`indep: 2026-02-27` MEANS Date 27 2 2026
GIVETH A DATE
`indep: 2028-02-27` MEANS Date 27 2 2028
GIVETH A DATE
`indep: 2026-12-30` MEANS Date 30 12 2026
GIVETH A DATE
`indep: 2027-01-02` MEANS Date 2 1 2027

GIVETH A `a moment`
`indep: moment 2026-03-05 10:15` MEANS
    `a moment` WITH
        `day`    IS Date 5 3 2026
        `hour`   IS 10
        `minute` IS 15
GIVETH A MAYBE `a moment`
`indep: 2026-03-05 10:15` MEANS JUST `indep: moment 2026-03-05 10:15`
GIVETH A `a moment`
`indep: moment 2026-03-02 23:30` MEANS
    `a moment` WITH
        `day`    IS Date 2 3 2026
        `hour`   IS 23
        `minute` IS 30
GIVETH A MAYBE `a moment`
`indep: 2026-03-02 23:30` MEANS JUST `indep: moment 2026-03-02 23:30`
GIVETH A `a moment`
`indep: moment 2028-03-01 23:30` MEANS
    `a moment` WITH
        `day`    IS Date 1 3 2028
        `hour`   IS 23
        `minute` IS 30
GIVETH A MAYBE `a moment`
`indep: 2028-03-01 23:30` MEANS JUST `indep: moment 2028-03-01 23:30`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a moment`
`indep: no moment` MEANS NOTHING

§ `(1) Do the Regulations apply to me?`

-- Argument order: information society service, cloud, search engine, marketplace,
-- provided in UK, head office in UK, UK representative, micro/small, OES.
-- RDSP (reg 1(3)(e), txt:117-119): a cloud computing service, UK head office, not small.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- An "online search engine" (reg 1(2), txt:107) is also a digital service.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: no` `indep: yes` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- Fork F-A: none of the three kinds -> not a digital service -> neither.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: no` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- Fork F-A left open by the provider.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: cannot say` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only as an RDSP, and only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
-- Micro or small enterprise (reg 1(3)(e)(ii), txt:119) -> not an RDSP.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- Not an information society service -> not a "digital service" (reg 1(2), txt:94).
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` FALSE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- Not provided in the UK (reg 1(3)(e) "provides a digital service in the United Kingdom").
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- Outside the UK, no representative: fails reg 1(3)(e)(i) (txt:118) -> not an RDSP.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- Outside the UK, with a UK representative -> an RDSP.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- OES is a stated fact (Schedule 2; impossible for the model itself, see answers-first (1)).
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: no` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, as an OES only`
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, as an OES and as an RDSP`

§ `(6) Must I nominate a UK representative? (reg 14A)`

-- Argument order: information society service, cloud, search, marketplace, offered in UK, head office in UK, micro/small.
-- Head office outside the UK, offers a digital service in the UK, not small (14A(1), txt:3-5).
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must nominate a UK representative in writing and notify the Information Commission of its name and contact details`
-- Small or micro: 14A(1)(b).
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
-- Head office in the UK: 14A(1)(a).
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
-- Not offering in the UK: 14A(1)(a).
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
-- Not a digital service: not a "digital service provider" (reg 1(2), txt:95).
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `indep: no` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `indep: cannot say` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

§ `(2) Must I notify, and whom?`

-- Argument order: ISS, cloud, search, marketplace, provided in UK, HQ in UK, rep, small, OES,
-- actual adverse effect, substantial impact, information to assess, significant impact on essential service, RDSP incident affecting me.
-- RDSP, an incident (actual adverse effect), substantial, with information to assess -> notify (reg 12(3), txt:332).
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I must notify`
-- Not substantial -> no duty.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- No access to information to assess substantiality -> reg 12(4) (txt:333): no duty.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- No actual adverse effect -> not an "incident" (reg 1(2), txt:103).
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- Outside the UK without a representative: not an RDSP (fork F-G, my reading) -> no reg 12(3) duty.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- Outside the UK with a UK representative: an RDSP -> notify.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I must notify`
-- Small -> not an RDSP.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- Cloud computing service: no -> not a digital service -> no duty.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: no` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- Cloud computing service: cannot say -> conditional.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: cannot say` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I must notify only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
-- OES with a NIS incident (reg 11(1), txt:285).
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `indep: no` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I must notify`
-- Whom: an RDSP notifies the Information Commission (reg 12(3); reg 3(2), txt:154).
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Information Commission`
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Information Commission`
-- Whom: no duty -> no one.
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no one under these Regulations`
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no one under these Regulations`
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `indep: cannot say` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Information Commission, if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
-- Whom: an OES notifies its designated competent authority (reg 11(1)).
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `indep: no` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my designated competent authority`

§ `(3) By when? 72 hours, inclusive (reg 12(6)(a), txt:342; reg 11(3)(b)(i), txt:299)`

-- The outer limit is awareness + 72 hours, to the minute.
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 EQUALS `indep: 2026-03-05 10:15`
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `indep: OES duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 EQUALS `indep: 2026-03-05 10:15`
-- Across the end of a non-leap February (2026): 27 Feb + 3 days = 2 March.
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-02-27` 23 30 EQUALS `indep: 2026-03-02 23:30`
-- Across the end of a leap February (2028): 27 Feb + 3 days = 1 March.
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2028-02-27` 23 30 EQUALS `indep: 2028-03-01 23:30`
-- Reg 12(9): "without undue delay" only, no hour limit (txt:353).
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `indep: 12(9) duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 EQUALS `indep: no moment`
-- Edges, aware 2026-03-02 10:15 (RDSP): 0h, 71h59m, 72h00m within; 72h01m, 73h late.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 `indep: 2026-03-05` 10 14 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 `indep: 2026-03-05` 10 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 `indep: 2026-03-05` 10 16 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 `indep: 2026-03-05` 11 15 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Same edges for an OES.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: OES duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 `indep: 2026-03-05` 10 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: OES duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 `indep: 2026-03-05` 10 16 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Midnight: aware 23:59, notified 72h later at 23:59 (in time), one minute later 00:00 next day (late).
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 23 59 `indep: 2026-03-05` 23 59 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 23 59 `indep: 2026-03-06` 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Year end: aware 2026-12-30 12:00.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-12-30` 12 0 `indep: 2027-01-02` 12 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: RDSP duty` `indep: 2026-12-30` 12 0 `indep: 2027-01-02` 12 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reg 12(9): no 72-hour limit to be within.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `indep: 12(9) duty` `indep: 2026-03-02` 10 15 `indep: 2026-03-06` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `(5) The most I can be penalised (reg 18(6), txt:527-531; reg 18(7)(a), txt:533-539)`

-- Argument order: duty, what happened, reading (late RDSP only), enforcement notice position, authority's view.
-- No failure, no penalty.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I notified in time with the required information` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: no EN` `indep: undetermined` EQUALS `no penalty: there was no failure to notify`
-- Did not notify (17(2)(b)), no enforcement notice -> material (18(7)(a)(ii)); ceiling by the authority's view.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: no EN` `indep: significant` EQUALS `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: no EN` `indep: not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: no EN` `indep: undetermined` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds, or up to 17,000,000 pounds if the authority determines it has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
-- Enforcement notice served but required no steps -> still material under 18(7)(a)(ii).
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: EN no steps` `indep: not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
-- Enforcement notice required steps, I took them in time -> neither limb of 18(7)(a) -> not material -> 1,000,000 whatever the authority's view.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: EN steps taken` `indep: significant` EQUALS `up to 1,000,000 pounds: not a material contravention`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: EN steps taken` `indep: not significant` EQUALS `up to 1,000,000 pounds: not a material contravention`
-- Enforcement notice required steps, not taken in time -> material under 18(7)(a)(i).
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: EN steps not taken` `indep: significant` EQUALS `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
-- Notified in time without the 12(5) information -> 17(2)(c) -> material.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I notified in time, but without the required information` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: no EN` `indep: not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
-- Late RDSP notice, fork F-E. My reading (literal): 12(6) is not named in 17(2) -> no penalty for lateness alone.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I notified, but more than 72 hours after the clock started` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: no EN` `indep: significant` EQUALS `no penalty under regulation 18 on reading B: lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
-- Late RDSP notice, the other reading: a failure to notify under 12(3) -> 17(2)(b) -> material.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I notified, but more than 72 hours after the clock started` `indep: reading late is a 12(3) failure` `indep: no EN` `indep: not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I notified, but more than 72 hours after the clock started` `indep: reading late is a 12(3) failure` `indep: EN steps taken` `indep: significant` EQUALS `up to 1,000,000 pounds: not a material contravention`
-- Late OES notice: 17(1)(c) names 11(3), which holds the 72 hours (txt:299, 465) -> material ON EITHER READING; the reading input is for RDSPs only.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: OES duty` `I notified, but more than 72 hours after the clock started` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: no EN` `indep: not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: OES duty` `I notified, but more than 72 hours after the clock started` `indep: reading late is a 12(3) failure` `indep: no EN` `indep: significant` EQUALS `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: OES duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: no EN` `indep: not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
-- An OES that did not notify under reg 12(9) at all: 17(1)(d) names "notify an incident as required by
-- regulation 12(9)" (txt:466), inside "(a) to (d)" of 18(7)(a)(ii)(aa) -> material. The source answers this
-- case even though 12(9) has no hour limit and no content list.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: 12(9) duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading 12(6) not listed` `indep: no EN` `indep: not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`

§ `Added after step E (expected values from answers-first (1) and (5), written before the encoding was opened)`

-- Any one of the three kinds is a digital service (reg 1(2), txt:94): a marketplace alone; a search engine with "cannot say" on cloud.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: no` `indep: no` `indep: yes` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: cannot say` `indep: yes` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- The micro/small exclusion is in the RDSP definition only (reg 1(3)(e)(ii)); an OES stays an OES.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `indep: yes` `indep: no` `indep: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, as an OES only`
-- The F-E reading matters only for lateness: a total failure to notify, or a 12(5) content failure, is listed (17(2)(b), (c)) on either reading.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I did not notify at all` `indep: reading late is a 12(3) failure` `indep: no EN` `indep: not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `indep: RDSP duty` `I notified in time, but without the required information` `indep: reading late is a 12(3) failure` `indep: no EN` `indep: significant` EQUALS `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`

-- STEP E: comparison with the encoder's NOTES.md and nis-tests.l4, read after every assertion above was written and run.
-- No assertion fails. On every point tested, the encoding gives the answer decided from the source.
-- The encoder's fork labels are the reverse of mine for the late-RDSP-notice fork: their reading A
-- (late = failure under 12(3)) is my reading B; their reading B (12(6) not listed in 17(2)) is my
-- reading A. The encoding computes both; NOTES.md declines to state "no penalty for lateness". I
-- would state the literal reading as the stronger one, because 17(1)(c) names 11(3) whole (content
-- AND the 72 hours, txt:299, 465) while 17(2)(c) names only 12(5) (content, txt:474), and 12(6)
-- (txt:341-343) appears nowhere in 17(2). The text is still open; neither side is wrong.
-- Differences of emphasis, none of which changes an output:
-- 1. Reg 12(6)(b) (cross-border sufficiency, txt:343) is unlisted in 17(2) exactly as 12(6)(a) is.
--    The penalty question's input "I notified in time, but without the required information" cannot
--    say WHICH information was missing, so a notice that had every 12(5) item but not enough for the
--    cross-border determination is answered as a 17(2)(c) material contravention, which the literal
--    reading does not support. Untestable through the baseline; a finding about the input.
-- 2. OES: the encoding asks it as a fact (Schedule 2 deferred). On the source, no Schedule 2 kind
--    (txt:621-973) is an AI model service, so an AI provider is an OES only for some other service it
--    runs (e.g. a DNS resolver); the OES @desc does not say so.
-- 3. NOTES.md says "the UK text sets no numeric threshold". What the deposit shows is that Article 4 of
--    EU Reg 2018/151 is a row of dots in the AID text (eur:15-16); "the deposited aid text" is the
--    accurate scope, since the official text was not read.
-- Untestable through the baseline (no exported question): reg 14A(3) time limit (deferred, F13);
-- whether a 14A failure is a "material contravention" (my F-D: 17(2)(da) falls outside "(a) to (d)",
-- so max 1,000,000); enforceability of 14A against a non-UK provider that never nominates (my F-G,
-- their F7, recorded as an open question); the notification CONTENT lists (11(3)(a), 12(5), 12(6)(b),
-- inert in the encoding); "without undue delay" before 72 hours (F5, outer limit only, as I read it).
